{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/ben/github/toulmin/evals/toulmin/variants/ask-only/skills/toulmin\n\n# Writing the piece\n\nBefore you write, ask the user for what you are missing. Send one message with at most five questions, the most useful first. Ask only what would change the piece and what the request does not already answer. When the answers come back, write the piece as you normally would, and hand it over. When the user does not know something, write without it and do not guess.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Cover letter for a 52-year-old applying for office manager at a 3-dentist dental practice (supervises 9). Background: 11 years office manager at vet clinic (4 vets, 14 staff), scheduling, billing, led paper-to-software move in 2014, cut 90+ day unpaid invoices from ~$38k to ~$9k over last 3 years. 7-year gap caring for mother (died last spring); managed her insurance claims and 6 specialists. No Dentrix; used AVImark. Under 300 words."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"029022f2-b422-4115-a10b-e21f1670f964","uuid":"af83d533-83ec-4b5f-b7f7-7245bd495743","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:20:10.837Z","isSynthetic":true}
