{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JjHnnoqQGDzPPMDAXa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written it. On the staffing question I described the clinic's size but didn't say you supervised the 14 staff.\n\n<final_document>\nDear Dr. Pierce,\n\nI am applying for the office manager position at Brookside Family Dental. For eleven years I was office manager at a veterinary clinic with four veterinarians and 14 staff, and I would like to bring that experience to your practice.\n\nAt the clinic I handled scheduling and billing, and in 2014 I managed the clinic's move from paper records to AVImark practice software. In my last three years there, I brought unpaid invoices over 90 days down from about $38,000 to $9,000.\n\nI spent the last seven years caring for my mother until her death last spring. During that time I managed her insurance claims and coordinated her appointments with six specialists. It gave me a close look at insurance billing and scheduling from the patient's side, and a clear sense of how much a well-run front office matters to the people it serves.\n\nYour posting lists Dentrix. My experience is with AVImark, so I have enrolled in the Dentrix online training course, about 20 hours, and will complete it before my first day. Having already taken a whole clinic from paper to software, I am confident I can learn a new system quickly.\n\nI would welcome the chance to talk with you about how I could help keep Brookside running smoothly for your dentists, your staff, and your patients. Thank you for your consideration.\n\nSincerely,\nLinda Marsh\n</final_document>\n\nIt's about 240 words. Before you send it, check two things:\n\n- **Staffing:** If you did any hiring, training or staff scheduling at the clinic, add a sentence about it. The job is mainly about managing 9 people, so that would be the strongest addition you could make.\n- **Dentrix:** The letter says you will complete the 